{"availability":"available","full":"erwintrg/job-reply-classifier","name":"job-reply-classifier","description":"Watches several Gmail inboxes for replies to job applications: regex pre-filter, Claude Haiku classification (receipt, positive, negative, question), quiet hours and routing. Offline demo.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-02T23:28:04Z","updated":"2026-10-03T00:00:43Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":["automation","claude","email-classification","gmail-api","llm","python"],"demo":"https://developers.google.com/oauthplayground","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:40.311Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:40.311Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:40.311Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T06:45:40.311Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Watches several Gmail inboxes for replies to job applications, has Claude Haiku sort each reply (receipt, positive, negative, question, or not job related) and routes the result: receipts are logged quietly, interview invitations and questions ping you right away, rejections that arrive at night wait until the morning.","It is built for anyone running a job search, a recruiting pipeline or a hiring inbox. This repo is a sanitized rebuild of a watcher that runs in production on real inboxes: the production version checks two Gmail accounts every two minutes and posts to a task board that an assistant agent works from. Here the private parts are replaced with pluggable sources, classifiers and sinks, plus an offline demo that runs without any account or key."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/erwintrg/job-reply-classifier/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"ce5dbb4fea00c6a05958225ca978951b4e6b8712f92815c4e7cff178afd345e2","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:40.450Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:40.450Z","projectInsights":{"version":